---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="What CC3PO AI Builders collects, why, and what you can ask us to delete. CC3PO LLC."
>
  <div class="container wrap">
    <div class="badge">Policy</div>
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      CC3PO AI Builders · CC3PO LLC · Last updated: November 2026
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      We collect what we need to run the program. We don't sell it, we don't
      share it, and we don't add you to lists you didn't ask for. You can ask
      us to delete it, any time, and we'll do it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      CC3PO LLC ("CC3PO", "we"). Operated by Carlos Cabrales.
      Contact: <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a> ·
      209-701-1137
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>From the welcome &amp; intake form:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name, email, phone, city</li>
      <li>What you do (business owner, developer, student, etc.)</li>
      <li>What you're building or running</li>
      <li>Your coding comfort level</li>
      <li>Access needs (optional, and it never affects whether you get a seat)</li>
      <li>How you heard about us</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>From the assessments:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your knowledge assessment score</li>
      <li>Your self-assessment responses</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>From the media release:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Whether you consent to photos, video, name use, and testimonials</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>From attending:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Attendance records, per session</li>
      <li>Feedback forms</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>From the labs: nothing</h2>
    <p>
      The demo runs on our own hardware. We do not collect what you type during
      sessions. If you put data into a third-party tool yourself (ChatGPT,
      Claude, Gemini), that tool's privacy policy applies — which is exactly
      why we use synthetic and public data in class.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights (California residents)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, the CCPA/CPRA gives you the right to
      know what personal information we hold about you, to request deletion,
      to correct it, and to opt out of any sale or sharing of it. We do not
      sell or share personal information as those terms are defined under the
      CCPA, so there is nothing to opt out of. To exercise any right, email
      <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a> and we will
      respond within 45 days.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Application and intake records are kept for 24 months, then deleted.
      Attendance and assessment records are kept for 24 months so we can
      report outcomes honestly to sponsors and funders. Media consent records
      are kept for 24 months. Deletion requests are honoured immediately on
      receipt, except where a record must be retained for legal or insurance
      purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
      Carlos Cabrales, and the volunteers who help run a session — for
      attendance and safety. We share your name and employer with a sponsor
      only in aggregate (for example, "11 business owners attended"), never
      individually, unless you ask us to introduce you. We do not sell or
      share personal information with third parties for their own marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>Your information, your call</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to delete your information, correct it, or stop using it
      for any purpose. Email <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a>
      and we will do it.
    </p>

    <p class="foot">
      Contact: Carlos Cabrales · CC3PO LLC ·
      <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a> · 209-701-1137
    </p>
  </div>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<style>
  .wrap { padding: 90px 0 60px; max-width: 720px; }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; background: rgba(16,185,129,0.1); color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16,185,129,0.2); border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 6px 16px; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lead { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 14px 0 34px; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 12px 0; }
  ul { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 12px 0 12px 20px; }
  li { margin: 5px 0; }
  strong { color: var(--text); }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .foot {
    margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
